01:03:49.860 --> 01:03:53.820
That's why you saw what TikTok had to go through

1542
01:03:53.820 --> 01:03:54.710
during that summer.

1543
01:03:54.710 --> 01:03:56.400
I mean, there was a lot of political upheaval

1544
01:03:56.400 --> 01:03:58.110
that it unfortunately had to go through

1545
01:03:58.110 --> 01:04:01.737
with it being canceled like every six weeks, or I think,

1546
01:04:01.737 --> 01:04:03.090
"It's gonna be banned tomorrow.

1547
01:04:03.090 --> 01:04:05.100
Make sure you save all your videos."

1548
01:04:05.100 --> 01:04:05.933
So there was that,

1549
01:04:05.933 --> 01:04:09.770
but there was just this crazy onboarding

1550
01:04:09.770 --> 01:04:11.690
as consumers or creators, right?

1551
01:04:11.690 --> 01:04:13.840
People would join just to watch

1552
01:04:13.840 --> 01:04:16.280
and then be inspired by something they see

1553
01:04:16.280 --> 01:04:19.140
and then decide, "Well, now I wanna create content as well."

1554
01:04:19.140 --> 01:04:21.120
That's exactly what happened to me.

1555
01:04:21.120 --> 01:04:24.820
I was inspired by so many of the things that I was seeing.

1556
01:04:24.820 --> 01:04:27.160
Politically, from an activism standpoint,

1557
01:04:27.160 --> 01:04:29.360
and as just a content creator,

1558
01:04:29.360 --> 01:04:31.520
I wanted to create beautiful things.

1559
01:04:31.520 --> 01:04:33.690
And that's ultimately why I decided

1560
01:04:33.690 --> 01:04:35.537
to start throwing out content there.

1561
01:04:35.537 --> 01:04:36.850
Right.
Was not pretty

1562
01:04:36.850 --> 01:04:37.900
in the beginning though, for sure.

1563
01:04:37.900 --> 01:04:40.360
No, but it kind of went crazy viral

1564
01:04:40.360 --> 01:04:42.120
from the get-go didn't it?

1565
01:04:42.120 --> 01:04:46.620
Yes. So I posted like a potato dish.

1566
01:04:46.620 --> 01:04:48.860
That was very not pretty.

1567
01:04:48.860 --> 01:04:50.640
It was like with my really crappy phone

1568
01:04:50.640 --> 01:04:53.460
and you can hear Anthony giving a piano lesson

1569
01:04:53.460 --> 01:04:54.503
in the background.

1570
01:04:55.520 --> 01:04:57.600
And I didn't know how to use the app.

1571
01:04:57.600 --> 01:04:59.770
So you'll see like all of my captions

1572
01:04:59.770 --> 01:05:02.780
are like, you know, overlapping on top of one another.

1573
01:05:02.780 --> 01:05:04.950
It was really not well done.

1574
01:05:04.950 --> 01:05:06.560
But, it went viral.

1575
01:05:06.560 --> 01:05:09.130
It has over, I think 1.6 million views.

1576
01:05:09.130 --> 01:05:11.700
And a lot of people really liked it.

1577
01:05:11.700 --> 01:05:14.830
And that's how TikTok gets ya, you know?

1578
01:05:14.830 --> 01:05:16.670
They're like, "Here's a little taste

1579
01:05:16.670 --> 01:05:18.610
of what it's like to go viral."

1580
01:05:18.610 --> 01:05:21.490
And if you can ride that wave,

1581
01:05:21.490 --> 01:05:24.820
I mean, it really can sort of shoot you up

1582
01:05:24.820 --> 01:05:27.500
to, you know, superstardom on TikTok.

1583
01:05:27.500 --> 01:05:28.333
Mm-hmm.

1584
01:05:28.333 --> 01:05:31.330
How much time have you spent with your lawyer mind,

1585
01:05:31.330 --> 01:05:34.430
like trying to dissect that and be strategic versus,

1586
01:05:34.430 --> 01:05:36.640
'cause there's a tension between,

1587
01:05:36.640 --> 01:05:38.530
you know, one of the reasons I suspect

1588
01:05:38.530 --> 01:05:40.870
that that original video went viral

1589
01:05:40.870 --> 01:05:44.130
is not in spite of,

1590
01:05:44.130 --> 01:05:46.560
you know, Anthony playing piano in the background,

1591
01:05:46.560 --> 01:05:49.150
but in large part, because of that, like there's a realness,

1592
01:05:49.150 --> 01:05:50.830
there's an authenticity to it.

1593
01:05:50.830 --> 01:05:54.780
That rawness, that honesty is what people respond to.

1594
01:05:54.780 --> 01:05:57.710
And as you become more professional with it,

1595
01:05:57.710 --> 01:06:01.040
and you've got three cameras and the whole thing going on,

1596
01:06:01.040 --> 01:06:02.260
you have to be mindful

1597
01:06:02.260 --> 01:06:04.210
of maintaining the heart and integrity

1598
01:06:04.210 --> 01:06:05.270
of what it is you're doing.

1599
01:06:05.270 --> 01:06:07.330
Otherwise, it doesn't matter how pretty it looks

1600
01:06:07.330 --> 01:06:09.540
because it's the honesty

1601
01:06:11.260 --> 01:06:13.513
that is keeping people connected to you.

1602
01:06:14.550 --> 01:06:17.790
I think that, again, as a lawyer,

1603
01:06:17.790 --> 01:06:21.010
I automatically tend to take as much data

1604
01:06:21.010 --> 01:06:23.430
as I have available to me and try and crunch it

1605
01:06:23.430 --> 01:06:24.710
and come up with solutions

1606
01:06:24.710 --> 01:06:26.770
and conclusions to my next decision.

1607
01:06:26.770 --> 01:06:28.540
That's like second nature,

1608
01:06:28.540 --> 01:06:29.410
right?
Right.

1609
01:06:29.410 --> 01:06:34.170
And the algorithm, as you put it, is a big black box.

1610
01:06:34.170 --> 01:06:37.160
I probably follow multiple TikTok accounts

1611
01:06:37.160 --> 01:06:39.670
that purport to understand the algorithm

1612
01:06:39.670 --> 01:06:41.390
or hack the algorithm.

1613
01:06:41.390 --> 01:06:43.660
And in the very beginning,

1614
01:06:43.660 --> 01:06:45.480
I think I was driven very much

1615
01:06:45.480 --> 01:06:48.950
by a need to maximize what I had,

1616
01:06:48.950 --> 01:06:50.447
this feeling of FOMO, right?

1617
01:06:50.447 --> 01:06:53.093
"Oh God, I gotta do another viral video.

1618
01:06:53.093 --> 01:06:56.450
You know, I can't let up on the accelerator."

1619
01:06:56.450 --> 01:06:57.860
And that was really my thinking.

1620
01:06:57.860 --> 01:06:58.810
And as a result of that,

1621
01:06:58.810 --> 01:07:01.690
I probably spent way too much time

1622
01:07:01.690 --> 01:07:03.517
trying to really understand,

1623
01:07:03.517 --> 01:07:05.260
"Okay, well, if I tweak just this

1624
01:07:05.260 --> 01:07:07.210
or if I post it this exact time,

1625
01:07:07.210 --> 01:07:10.190
or if I, you know, make sure that my phone

1626
01:07:10.190 --> 01:07:11.690
is angled this way, you know,

1627
01:07:11.690 --> 01:07:13.347
maybe I can get more views."

1628
01:07:14.280 --> 01:07:17.460
And ultimately, I think I got to a point

1629
01:07:17.460 --> 01:07:18.910
where I said, "You know what?

1630
01:07:20.060 --> 01:07:22.290
My content is who I am.

1631
01:07:22.290 --> 01:07:24.480
It's an extrapolation of who I am.

1632
01:07:24.480 --> 01:07:27.140
And other people will like it, or they won't like it.

1633
01:07:27.140 --> 01:07:31.720
And I can't spend too much time trying to adjust my person

1634
01:07:31.720 --> 01:07:35.050
to make sure that I'm liked by the most number of people."

1635
01:07:35.050 --> 01:07:37.450
You have to be happy with yourself first, right?

1636
01:07:37.450 --> 01:07:39.780
And it's the same thing with my content.

1637
01:07:39.780 --> 01:07:41.690
I was also given the sort of,

1638
01:07:41.690 --> 01:07:43.360
you know, cautionary warning

1639
01:07:43.360 --> 01:07:45.360
of, "Well, if you stop using your phone

1640
01:07:45.360 --> 01:07:47.420
and you replace it with a DSLR,

1641
01:07:47.420 --> 01:07:50.100
you know, it might be too professional

1642
01:07:50.100 --> 01:07:51.350
for the TikTok audience."

1643
01:07:51.350 --> 01:07:55.360
And I'm like, "I get that, but that's what I want.

1644
01:07:55.360 --> 01:07:56.770
I want it to be beautiful.

1645
01:07:56.770 --> 01:07:59.680
I want it to be as beautiful as possible."

1646
01:07:59.680 --> 01:08:00.513
And a lot of people,

1647
01:08:00.513 --> 01:08:01.747
they would show up on my TikTok and be like,

1648
01:08:01.747 --> 01:08:02.820
"Oh, I didn't know I was paying

1649
01:08:02.820 --> 01:08:05.090
for premier TikTok experience." (chuckles)

1650
01:08:05.090 --> 01:08:06.640
You know? And I liked that.

1651
01:08:06.640 --> 01:08:11.050
I like creating the most beautiful thing that I can create.

1652
01:08:11.050 --> 01:08:13.020
And it's constantly pushing me

1653
01:08:13.020 --> 01:08:15.490
to create something even more beautiful,

1654
01:08:15.490 --> 01:08:18.790
more revealing, more engaging.

1655
01:08:18.790 --> 01:08:22.130
How do I make this even more compelling?

1656
01:08:22.130 --> 01:08:24.830
And so I like that sort of challenge.

1657
01:08:24.830 --> 01:08:28.430
But it's not something that I'm as obsessed with

1658
01:08:28.430 --> 01:08:29.583
as I was in the beginning.

1659
01:08:29.583 --> 01:08:31.100
Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm.

1660
01:08:31.100 --> 01:08:34.550
Yeah. As long as you maintain the heart at the center of it.

1661
01:08:34.550 --> 01:08:36.060
Of course you want it to be beautiful,

1662
01:08:36.060 --> 01:08:38.740
but it can never come at the cost of that.

1663
01:08:38.740 --> 01:08:39.573
Totally.

1664
01:08:39.573 --> 01:08:41.940
And I think that's what my voiceovers do, you know?

1665
01:08:41.940 --> 01:08:44.610
Is okay, whatever you're seeing,

1666
01:08:44.610 --> 01:08:46.510
which is, you know, delicious food

1667
01:08:46.510 --> 01:08:49.370
and really pretty, you know, bulky and all that stuff.

1668
01:08:49.370 --> 01:08:51.190
You're always getting my voice,

1669
01:08:51.190 --> 01:08:53.320
and you're always getting my story

1670
01:08:53.320 --> 01:08:54.650
and what I'm talking about.

1671
01:08:54.650 --> 01:08:58.150
And now with, you know, sort of my Korean ante videos,

1672
01:08:58.150 --> 01:08:59.750
now they're getting literally me,

1673
01:08:59.750 --> 01:09:02.180
I'm sitting there trying to feed you food.

1674
01:09:02.180 --> 01:09:03.013
Right.

1675
01:09:03.013 --> 01:09:06.295
So in this three act structure that I keep coming back to,

1676
01:09:06.295 --> 01:09:07.200
(Joanne laughs)
food blogger

1677
01:09:07.200 --> 01:09:10.800
then sort of advocate activist in the second stage.

1678
01:09:10.800 --> 01:09:14.970
And then, you know, with the tick talk evolution

1679
01:09:14.970 --> 01:09:17.720
that you're currently in,

1680
01:09:17.720 --> 01:09:22.720
another piece of that is not just giving voice

1681
01:09:23.180 --> 01:09:26.310
to the Korean-American experience,

1682
01:09:26.310 --> 01:09:31.310
but also this self-help, you know, sort of experience-based

1683
01:09:31.610 --> 01:09:34.150
life advice, aspect of it?
Mm-hmm.

1684
01:09:34.150 --> 01:09:38.390
That, correct me if I'm wrong, feels, or I understand,

1685
01:09:38.390 --> 01:09:42.024
is in some part inspired by you having a nephew, right?

1686
01:09:42.024 --> 01:09:42.857
Yes.

1687
01:09:42.857 --> 01:09:44.047
And so I'm watching these videos

1688
01:09:44.047 --> 01:09:47.390
and I'm thinking, oh, she's just talking to her nephew.

1689
01:09:47.390 --> 01:09:49.440
Like that's who she has in mind

1690
01:09:49.440 --> 01:09:51.100
when she's speaking to the camera,

1691
01:09:51.100 --> 01:09:53.082
she's really addressing him personally.

1692
01:09:53.082 --> 01:09:54.260
Yep. Yep.

1693
01:09:54.260 --> 01:09:56.820
So I'm addressing the 13 year old, 16 year old,

1694
01:09:56.820 --> 01:09:59.813
19 year old, 25 year old version of my nephew, Liam.

1695
01:10:01.560 --> 01:10:02.560
My younger brother,

1696
01:10:02.560 --> 01:10:05.590
who's probably one of my most favorite persons,

1697
01:10:05.590 --> 01:10:07.950
only surpassed by his son, Liam. (laughs)

1698
01:10:07.950 --> 01:10:10.040
He is three years old right now.

1699
01:10:10.040 --> 01:10:15.040
And he is just so fun and so talkative

1700
01:10:15.140 --> 01:10:18.420
and filled with laughter and joy.

1701
01:10:18.420 --> 01:10:20.897
And I started thinking,

1702
01:10:20.897 --> 01:10:24.590
"Man, I can't wait till he's old enough where we can have

1703
01:10:24.590 --> 01:10:27.850
these sort of really tough love conversations

1704
01:10:27.850 --> 01:10:31.907
about, oh, you know, "Gomo, this girl doesn't like me

1705
01:10:31.907 --> 01:10:33.920
and I don't know what to do about it."

1706
01:10:33.920 --> 01:10:36.770
Or "Gomo, this girl dumped me and I'm so sad,"

1707
01:10:36.770 --> 01:10:39.120
or, you know, "Gomo, I didn't get into the college

1708
01:10:39.120 --> 01:10:40.460
I wanted to."

1709
01:10:40.460 --> 01:10:42.780
And I was like, "Oh, I can't wait for these conversations.

1710
01:10:42.780 --> 01:10:44.500
And I know exactly what I would say

1711
01:10:44.500 --> 01:10:45.707
if he were sitting in front of me."

1712
01:10:45.707 --> 01:10:47.700
Right.
So yeah, that first one

1713
01:10:47.700 --> 01:10:50.300
was very much inspired by, "Okay, I can see Liam,

1714
01:10:50.300 --> 01:10:51.990
he's sitting across the dining table from me

1715
01:10:51.990 --> 01:10:53.430
and I'm cutting up a pear for him,

1716
01:10:53.430 --> 01:10:55.940
just like my mom used to do when I was sad.

1717
01:10:55.940 --> 01:10:57.370
And this is what I would tell him."

1718
01:10:57.370 --> 01:10:58.203
Right.

1719
01:10:58.203 --> 01:11:01.420
My favorite one is the one of you telling the story

1720
01:11:01.420 --> 01:11:04.879
about the boy who broke up with you in elementary school,

1721
01:11:04.879 --> 01:11:05.870
(Joanne laughs)

1722
01:11:05.870 --> 01:11:08.820
and then it ends with you in the business suit,

1723
01:11:08.820 --> 01:11:10.560
like being a bad-ass.

1724
01:11:10.560 --> 01:11:11.923
Yeah. You know?

1725
01:11:13.547 --> 01:11:15.110
You know, I was just trying to do something fun.

1726
01:11:15.110 --> 01:11:17.050
Like, hey, you know, like all tongue in cheek,

1727
01:11:17.050 --> 01:11:19.910
like obviously, like I don't hold a grudge against this kid,

1728
01:11:19.910 --> 01:11:20.743
(Rich laughs)
you know?

1729
01:11:20.743 --> 01:11:21.670
Like he was 13 years old.
Yeah.

1730
01:11:21.670 --> 01:11:25.480
But it was also again, designed to show people

1731
01:11:25.480 --> 01:11:28.810
who may not have had to deal with racism before,

1732
01:11:28.810 --> 01:11:30.990
how hurtful it can be.

1733
01:11:30.990 --> 01:11:34.390
And yeah, it's absolutely one of those memories

1734
01:11:34.390 --> 01:11:35.560
that I'll never forget

1735
01:11:35.560 --> 01:11:38.630
because he called me all those horrible names.

1736
01:11:38.630 --> 01:11:39.797
And I was like,

1737
01:11:39.797 --> 01:11:42.260
"I thought we were gonna be boyfriend and girlfriend.

1738
01:11:42.260 --> 01:11:44.400
And now you're calling me these horrible names."

1739
01:11:44.400 --> 01:11:45.233
Yeah.

1740
01:11:46.700 --> 01:11:49.490
What's cool about the Liam story is that,

1741
01:11:49.490 --> 01:11:52.477
because you're his aunt and not his mother,

1742
01:11:52.477 --> 01:11:55.220
you probably will be able to have those conversations.

1743
01:11:55.220 --> 01:11:58.267
Like the mom or the dad always thinks like,

1744
01:11:58.267 --> 01:12:01.710
"Oh, I can't wait for those types of exchanges,

1745
01:12:01.710 --> 01:12:05.331
but the kids never (speaker voice drowned with laugher)

1746
01:12:05.331 --> 01:12:06.164
(both laugh)
Yeah.

1747
01:12:06.164 --> 01:12:06.997
You know, they can't hear it.

1748
01:12:06.997 --> 01:12:08.810
They can't always hear it from the parent, you know?

1749
01:12:08.810 --> 01:12:11.100
Well, I think that was kind of the idea too,

1750
01:12:11.100 --> 01:12:15.380
is I can be a little bit more free about what I would say

1751
01:12:15.380 --> 01:12:18.670
because I am the cool aunt, as opposed to,

1752
01:12:18.670 --> 01:12:20.400
you know, the cuddly mom,

1753
01:12:20.400 --> 01:12:22.150
I'm never gonna be the cuddly aunt.

1754
01:12:22.150 --> 01:12:26.340
And you know, if you know a little bit about Korean culture,

1755
01:12:26.340 --> 01:12:29.730
Gomo is your father's sister

1756
01:12:29.730 --> 01:12:32.520
and emo is your mother's sister.

1757
01:12:32.520 --> 01:12:36.490
And your emo is again, very cuddly, sweet.

1758
01:12:36.490 --> 01:12:38.297
You know, like the sweet.

1759
01:12:38.297 --> 01:12:41.050
And gomo is oftentimes a little bit more reserved,

1760
01:12:41.050 --> 01:12:43.830
a little bit aloof, but way cooler.

1761
01:12:43.830 --> 01:12:45.390
And that was sort of the persona

1762
01:12:45.390 --> 01:12:48.160
that I'm trying to like, you know, put across,

1763
01:12:48.160 --> 01:12:50.707
which is, "Look, I'm not gonna tell you what you wanna hear.

1764
01:12:50.707 --> 01:12:52.390
I'm not gonna tell you, 'Oh, don't worry.

1765
01:12:52.390 --> 01:12:54.760
She'll like you in five days, don't worry.

1766
01:12:54.760 --> 01:12:55.710
Just keep trying.'

1767
01:12:55.710 --> 01:12:58.250
Or 'It's okay, that college was dumb

1768
01:12:58.250 --> 01:12:59.690
and you didn't wanna go there anyway.'

1769
01:12:59.690 --> 01:13:01.400
I'm not gonna give you that advice.

1770
01:13:01.400 --> 01:13:04.900
But, I do want you to feel empowered."

1771
01:13:04.900 --> 01:13:07.010
That is like the most important thing

1772
01:13:07.010 --> 01:13:08.740
out of these advice videos.

1773
01:13:08.740 --> 01:13:10.097
I'm always thinking,

1774
01:13:10.097 --> 01:13:13.210
"How can I communicate to a young person,

1775
01:13:13.210 --> 01:13:15.120
the power is in you?

1776
01:13:15.120 --> 01:13:16.510
You don't need to look to me.

1777
01:13:16.510 --> 01:13:18.500
You don't need to look to everyone around you,

1778
01:13:18.500 --> 01:13:19.698
it's inside of you."

1779
01:13:19.698 --> 01:13:20.531
Right.

1780
01:13:20.531 --> 01:13:22.070
And exposing the myths or the lies

1781
01:13:22.070 --> 01:13:23.930
behind a lot of self-help tropes.

1782
01:13:23.930 --> 01:13:25.127
Like the one where you're like,

1783
01:13:25.127 --> 01:13:27.460
"You know, that thing where they tell you,

1784
01:13:27.460 --> 01:13:29.690
you know, whatever doesn't kill you makes you stronger."

1785
01:13:29.690 --> 01:13:30.962
And you're like, "Fuck that."

1786
01:13:30.962 --> 01:13:31.920
(Joanne laughs)
Yow know like the knife

1787
01:13:31.920 --> 01:13:32.753
and all of that.

1788
01:13:32.753 --> 01:13:33.586
It's like truth talk.

1789
01:13:33.586 --> 01:13:34.490
Yes. Exactly.

1790
01:13:34.490 --> 01:13:35.760
With The Korean Vegan.

1791
01:13:35.760 --> 01:13:37.153
That's exactly right.
It's all going down.

1792
01:13:37.153 --> 01:13:40.100
So I never realized like that's what I would incorporate

1793
01:13:40.100 --> 01:13:42.054
into The Korean Vegan.

1794
01:13:42.054 --> 01:13:45.310
It's again, completely inspired by Liam.

1795
01:13:45.310 --> 01:13:48.910
Right. That's funny. Well, let's talk about Korean food.

1796
01:13:48.910 --> 01:13:53.040
Most Americans' relationship with Korean food

1797
