01:24:25.810 --> 01:24:27.477
But at the time I was like,

2050
01:24:27.477 --> 01:24:28.910
"You know what? You guys are the experts.

2051
01:24:28.910 --> 01:24:32.290
You tell me what will make my book a success.

2052
01:24:32.290 --> 01:24:34.830
And if you're telling me that we need to cut out the stories

2053
01:24:34.830 --> 01:24:38.420
and do more recipes and replace it with one big essay,

2054
01:24:38.420 --> 01:24:39.580
like I'll do that."

2055
01:24:39.580 --> 01:24:41.950
And then I signed up for TikTok.

2056
01:24:41.950 --> 01:24:45.960
And all of a sudden my stories were getting a lot of play.

2057
01:24:45.960 --> 01:24:47.530
And then they're like, "Do more of that."

2058
01:24:47.530 --> 01:24:48.363
Yeah.

2059
01:24:48.363 --> 01:24:50.330
They're like, "Actually remember the one that we cut?

2060
01:24:50.330 --> 01:24:51.830
Put it back in?
Yeah.

2061
01:24:51.830 --> 01:24:52.663
And then I got-

2062
01:24:52.663 --> 01:24:55.060
'Cause your book deal came way before TikTok, right?

2063
01:24:55.060 --> 01:24:57.373
It did. It came like almost two years before TikTok.

2064
01:24:57.373 --> 01:24:58.660
Wow!
Yeah. Mm-hmm.

2065
01:24:58.660 --> 01:25:00.280
So you've been working on this book for a long time.

2066
01:25:00.280 --> 01:25:02.820
Yes, this is what happens when you're a full-time lawyer

2067
01:25:02.820 --> 01:25:04.030
and a cookbook writer,

2068
01:25:04.030 --> 01:25:07.935
your editor becomes very nice and understanding and patient.

2069
01:25:07.935 --> 01:25:08.890
To a point.

2070
01:25:08.890 --> 01:25:09.957
Yes. To a point.

2071
01:25:09.957 --> 01:25:12.070
"Are we ever gonna put that book out?"

2072
01:25:12.070 --> 01:25:15.898
They were great. I mean, my editor and the whole team-

2073
01:25:15.898 --> 01:25:16.977
Was Lucia your editor?

2074
01:25:16.977 --> 01:25:18.750
Yes Lucia and-
She's fantastic.

2075
01:25:18.750 --> 01:25:19.583
She's wonderful.

2076
01:25:19.583 --> 01:25:20.570
And she gets me

2077
01:25:20.570 --> 01:25:23.880
and she is always been like the supportive mom,

2078
01:25:23.880 --> 01:25:25.030
like cheering me on,

2079
01:25:25.030 --> 01:25:28.630
like, you can do it just 10 more recipes or, you know, like,

2080
01:25:28.630 --> 01:25:31.080
and she's like, I love this story about your dad.

2081
01:25:31.080 --> 01:25:32.960
And she's just been wonderful.

2082
01:25:32.960 --> 01:25:35.930
And yeah, at first she was a little bit concerned

2083
01:25:35.930 --> 01:25:38.740
that the writing was gonna overtake the recipes.

2084
01:25:38.740 --> 01:25:41.520
But then when she saw how people responding to them,

2085
01:25:41.520 --> 01:25:43.012
she was like, yeah, let's go for it.

2086
01:25:43.012 --> 01:25:44.420
Yeah. I think it's the perfect blend.

2087
01:25:44.420 --> 01:25:46.460
Did you shoot the recipes yourself?

2088
01:25:46.460 --> 01:25:47.430
Yeah.
You did?

2089
01:25:47.430 --> 01:25:48.490
The whole book is me.

2090
01:25:48.490 --> 01:25:49.520
Wow.
Yeah.

2091
01:25:49.520 --> 01:25:51.760
The whole book is me, except for the picture of me.

2092
01:25:51.760 --> 01:25:52.717
My friend from high school took that picture of.

2093
01:25:52.717 --> 01:25:54.610
Yeah. That's really cool.

2094
01:25:54.610 --> 01:25:56.560
Mm-hmm.
I mean, there is,

2095
01:25:57.660 --> 01:25:59.820
I'm reminiscing because you know,

2096
01:25:59.820 --> 01:26:01.700
our cookbooks were born out of, you know,

2097
01:26:01.700 --> 01:26:03.030
our version of that story,

2098
01:26:03.030 --> 01:26:05.300
which is truly trying to figure this out

2099
01:26:05.300 --> 01:26:07.260
when I was the one who wanted to do this.

2100
01:26:07.260 --> 01:26:09.620
And, you know, she didn't go to culinary school either,

2101
01:26:09.620 --> 01:26:11.370
it was a process that kind of unfolded

2102
01:26:11.370 --> 01:26:12.850
organically over time.

2103
01:26:12.850 --> 01:26:14.020
Yeah we love your cookbooks. (laughs)

2104
01:26:14.020 --> 01:26:15.460
Thank you. Thank you.

2105
01:26:15.460 --> 01:26:17.060
We've had them, we love your cookbooks.

2106
01:26:17.060 --> 01:26:18.510
They're beautiful.

2107
01:26:18.510 --> 01:26:21.000
And I do remember like, you know,

2108
01:26:21.000 --> 01:26:24.120
when you went to Italy to kind of experience that

2109
01:26:24.120 --> 01:26:26.020
and bring home these recipes,

2110
01:26:26.020 --> 01:26:29.700
and I think that is a beautiful way of learning

2111
01:26:29.700 --> 01:26:33.490
how to broaden your culinary vocabulary.

2112
01:26:33.490 --> 01:26:34.760
We spent a lot of time in Italy

2113
01:26:34.760 --> 01:26:36.390
because Anthony is half Italian.

2114
01:26:36.390 --> 01:26:41.390
And so I always bring back ideas that infiltrate my kitchen

2115
01:26:41.760 --> 01:26:43.100
every time we come back from Rome.

2116
01:26:43.100 --> 01:26:47.000
Yeah. How is Anthony doing with all this?

2117
01:26:47.000 --> 01:26:48.760
Where's Anthony? Is he over there?

2118
01:26:48.760 --> 01:26:51.040
He's probably in the back room.

2119
01:26:51.040 --> 01:26:52.660
Oh, he's always on the phone right now.

2120
01:26:52.660 --> 01:26:55.950
He stepped out like, so you guys are in quarantine,

2121
01:26:55.950 --> 01:26:57.690
you're basically, you know,

2122
01:26:57.690 --> 01:27:00.380
it's just two of you in your home.

2123
01:27:00.380 --> 01:27:01.640
You're doing a million things.

2124
01:27:01.640 --> 01:27:03.180
He's doing what he's doing.

2125
01:27:03.180 --> 01:27:05.510
Meanwhile, you kind of explode, you know,

2126
01:27:05.510 --> 01:27:07.421
without ever leaving your apartment.

2127
01:27:07.421 --> 01:27:08.370
(Joanne laughs)
I mean, it has to be a bit

2128
01:27:08.370 --> 01:27:09.560
of a surreal experience.

2129
01:27:09.560 --> 01:27:11.913
Like how does that work with your relationship?

2130
01:27:12.810 --> 01:27:15.880
I could not be partnered with someone

2131
01:27:15.880 --> 01:27:20.880
who is more complimentary to who I am than Anthony.

2132
01:27:21.320 --> 01:27:24.690
And you know, this sounds terribly unromantic,

2133
01:27:24.690 --> 01:27:28.800
but I was very strategic about selecting my partner and-

2134
01:27:28.800 --> 01:27:31.380
It's so Korean. Of course you were.

2135
01:27:31.380 --> 01:27:34.760
Yeah, I was very strategic because I you know,

2136
01:27:34.760 --> 01:27:36.287
married for love the first time

2137
01:27:36.287 --> 01:27:38.830
and it didn't get me where I needed to go.

2138
01:27:38.830 --> 01:27:41.810
And so this time I was like, I need certain things

2139
01:27:41.810 --> 01:27:46.380
in my partner and Anthony is perfectly equipped

2140
01:27:46.380 --> 01:27:48.110
to handle everything.

2141
01:27:48.110 --> 01:27:50.070
So this is a good example.

2142
01:27:50.070 --> 01:27:52.950
You know, when I was invited to be on your podcast

2143
01:27:52.950 --> 01:27:54.600
and I remember I like poked him in the shoulder

2144
01:27:54.600 --> 01:27:55.647
at five in the morning, I'm like,

2145
01:27:55.647 --> 01:27:58.810
"I think that I'm going to be on the Ritual Podcast."

2146
01:27:58.810 --> 01:28:00.740
And he was like, super cool about it.

2147
01:28:00.740 --> 01:28:03.220
And he's like, "Congratulations, babe, you deserve it."

2148
01:28:03.220 --> 01:28:05.890
And like, that is very Anthony.

2149
01:28:05.890 --> 01:28:08.350
He's very even keeled.

2150
01:28:08.350 --> 01:28:10.460
You know, he's like this all the time

2151
01:28:10.460 --> 01:28:13.240
where I'm like completely all over the place up and down,

2152
01:28:13.240 --> 01:28:14.990
up and down emotionally.

2153
01:28:14.990 --> 01:28:18.970
And you know, he kind of helps to anchor me.

2154
01:28:18.970 --> 01:28:21.650
But the other thing that he does,

2155
01:28:21.650 --> 01:28:25.433
is he's always the one to ensure

2156
01:28:26.670 --> 01:28:30.340
that I am not undervaluing myself.

2157
01:28:30.340 --> 01:28:34.590
And that is a big, temptation for me is, you know,

2158
01:28:34.590 --> 01:28:37.930
sometimes it's hard to understand the difference between

2159
01:28:37.930 --> 01:28:40.790
low self-esteem and humility.

2160
01:28:40.790 --> 01:28:43.910
And so I'm constantly like I don't deserve this

2161
01:28:43.910 --> 01:28:46.620
or I don't deserve 2 million followers on TikTok.

2162
01:28:46.620 --> 01:28:49.150
Why am I getting so much attention?

2163
01:28:49.150 --> 01:28:51.070
Why am I being asked to be on this new show?

2164
01:28:51.070 --> 01:28:52.600
This doesn't make sense. I don't deserve it.

2165
01:28:52.600 --> 01:28:54.590
And I'm gonna totally F it up and suck.

2166
01:28:54.590 --> 01:28:56.410
And he's the one to tell me, "No,

2167
01:28:56.410 --> 01:28:58.680
you deserve all of it because you're extraordinary.

2168
01:28:58.680 --> 01:28:59.600
And you're amazing.

2169
01:28:59.600 --> 01:29:01.890
And you're gonna kick ass like you always do."

2170
01:29:01.890 --> 01:29:04.080
But he's not gonna do it in this like flowery way.

2171
01:29:04.080 --> 01:29:05.890
He's gonna do it like almost in like,

2172
01:29:05.890 --> 01:29:07.670
sort of a like tough love way.

2173
01:29:07.670 --> 01:29:08.503
Mm-hmm.

2174
01:29:08.503 --> 01:29:10.840
That's beautiful.
No we're great together.

2175
01:29:10.840 --> 01:29:11.673
Yeah. Yeah.

2176
01:29:11.673 --> 01:29:13.010
That's great.

2177
01:29:13.010 --> 01:29:17.960
Although with your, you know, very logical mind

2178
01:29:17.960 --> 01:29:20.260
and Korean sensibility,

2179
01:29:20.260 --> 01:29:22.880
you're also open to fortune tellers, right?

2180
01:29:22.880 --> 01:29:26.530
You got a story like... A crazy story.

2181
01:29:26.530 --> 01:29:27.513
About my mom.

2182
01:29:28.800 --> 01:29:31.192
What was the video where it was like

2183
01:29:31.192 --> 01:29:32.340
this person knew everything?

2184
01:29:32.340 --> 01:29:33.620
Oh yeah. The medium.

2185
01:29:33.620 --> 01:29:34.620
Yeah. Okay.

2186
01:29:34.620 --> 01:29:36.110
So yes, you're right.

2187
01:29:36.110 --> 01:29:38.926
That must offend your rational disposition.

2188
01:29:38.926 --> 01:29:39.759
You know what?

2189
01:29:39.759 --> 01:29:43.220
I have a healthy, healthy appreciation for the unknown,

2190
01:29:43.220 --> 01:29:44.053
if you will.

2191
01:29:44.053 --> 01:29:47.850
So I think, you know, what I've always believed is like,

2192
01:29:47.850 --> 01:29:49.730
you only know what you know, right?

2193
01:29:49.730 --> 01:29:52.620
And then there's this whole universe that you don't know.

2194
01:29:52.620 --> 01:29:54.750
So you have to respect that. Right?

2195
01:29:54.750 --> 01:29:56.500
And it's also fun knowing that

2196
01:29:56.500 --> 01:29:58.380
there's a whole bunch of stuff that you don't know

2197
01:29:58.380 --> 01:30:00.220
that you may discover, or you may not.

2198
01:30:00.220 --> 01:30:01.390
I think that's really fun.

2199
01:30:01.390 --> 01:30:03.760
And that's one of the beautiful things about life.

2200
01:30:03.760 --> 01:30:06.830
I've always been fascinated in ESP

2201
01:30:06.830 --> 01:30:08.550
or you know, psychics.

2202
01:30:08.550 --> 01:30:11.310
I mean, I wrote my like eighth grade research paper

2203
01:30:11.310 --> 01:30:15.194
on people who could bend spoons with their minds.

2204
01:30:15.194 --> 01:30:16.530
That's always something that I've loved.

2205
01:30:16.530 --> 01:30:20.050
And we like ended up, my girlfriend and I, you know,

2206
01:30:20.050 --> 01:30:22.080
she's a good friend.

2207
01:30:22.080 --> 01:30:24.660
She and I watched like the show called "Seatbelt Psychic,"

2208
01:30:24.660 --> 01:30:26.440
together, like really late at night,

2209
01:30:26.440 --> 01:30:28.710
we watched the whole show like in one sitting.

2210
01:30:28.710 --> 01:30:30.410
And I was like, I gotta meet this guy.

2211
01:30:30.410 --> 01:30:33.020
I gotta talk to him. I wanna talk to him.

2212
01:30:33.020 --> 01:30:35.790
And so I booked an appointment and yeah,

2213
01:30:35.790 --> 01:30:40.790
he had a lot of things to say that were pretty incredible.

2214
01:30:41.990 --> 01:30:44.870
I mean, I'm as skeptical as the next person

2215
01:30:44.870 --> 01:30:46.090
and I leave it to everyone

2216
01:30:46.090 --> 01:30:47.880
to make their own sort of judgment.

2217
01:30:47.880 --> 01:30:50.500
But I literally, as soon as I was done with that call,

2218
01:30:50.500 --> 01:30:51.830
I wrote everything down

2219
01:30:51.830 --> 01:30:53.320
'cause I didn't wanna forget anything,

2220
01:30:53.320 --> 01:30:55.030
like all the names and stuff like that.

2221
01:30:55.030 --> 01:30:57.770
I took like copious notes and then I re-typed them up

2222
01:30:57.770 --> 01:30:58.670
and everything.

2223
01:30:58.670 --> 01:31:01.140
And so there were a lot of things that he knew

2224
01:31:01.140 --> 01:31:02.690
that I just simply cannot explain how he knew.

2225
01:31:02.690 --> 01:31:04.590
Right, well, what made me think of it

2226
01:31:04.590 --> 01:31:06.260
was the fact that a lot of it

2227
01:31:06.260 --> 01:31:07.680
had to do with Anthony's father, right?

2228
01:31:07.680 --> 01:31:08.513
Yes.
Yeah.

2229
01:31:08.513 --> 01:31:12.717
Yeah. So we lost Anthony's father fairly early on.

2230
01:31:12.717 --> 01:31:15.330
And that was also one of the factors that I think

2231
01:31:15.330 --> 01:31:17.380
inspired him to pick up a copy of your book

2232
01:31:17.380 --> 01:31:19.100
and ultimately go plant-based.

2233
01:31:19.100 --> 01:31:21.360
Anthony's father had been dealing with a number

2234
01:31:21.360 --> 01:31:25.510
of autoimmune disease issues which ultimately led to his,

2235
01:31:25.510 --> 01:31:28.220
in my opinion, premature death, unfortunately.

2236
01:31:28.220 --> 01:31:30.130
He was otherwise a totally healthy, man.

2237
01:31:30.130 --> 01:31:32.820
He'd run like 50 marathons, was a tennis pro.

2238
01:31:32.820 --> 01:31:35.160
I mean, he was very healthy and active

2239
01:31:36.310 --> 01:31:40.440
and we lost him in 2015 before Anthony and I

2240
01:31:40.440 --> 01:31:41.370
were even married.

2241
01:31:41.370 --> 01:31:43.610
But you know, it took me like all of two minutes

2242
01:31:43.610 --> 01:31:45.020
to completely fall in love with him.

2243
01:31:45.020 --> 01:31:48.240
I mean, he's one of the most charming men ever.

2244
01:31:48.240 --> 01:31:53.240
And it was always very sad for me

2245
01:31:54.450 --> 01:31:57.550
that I didn't get to spend more time with him

2246
01:31:57.550 --> 01:32:01.830
in particular that he didn't get to see me run a marathon,

2247
01:32:01.830 --> 01:32:04.940
which, you know, he'd always been so encouraging to

2248
01:32:04.940 --> 01:32:07.800
you know, just run three miles, you can do a 5k, you know.

2249
01:32:07.800 --> 01:32:09.960
I remember I ran my first race and I come home.

2250
01:32:09.960 --> 01:32:13.200
There's huge batch of blueberry muffins waiting for me.

2251
01:32:13.200 --> 01:32:14.940
And he was so proud of me.

2252
01:32:14.940 --> 01:32:19.940
And I always wanted to show him that I valued his love

2253
01:32:21.210 --> 01:32:22.870
and passion for running.

2254
01:32:22.870 --> 01:32:27.440
And, you know, so I ultimately run my first marathon in 2017

2255
01:32:27.440 --> 01:32:29.380
and I'd always wondered like, "Oh, can he see me

2256
01:32:29.380 --> 01:32:31.800
like crossing the finish line, in heaven?

2257
01:32:31.800 --> 01:32:32.740
Is he watching me?"

2258
01:32:32.740 --> 01:32:35.140
And I remember I actually had a dream about it.

2259
01:32:35.140 --> 01:32:38.900
Like I dreamt shortly after finishing my first marathon

2260
01:32:38.900 --> 01:32:40.000
that we were all in a car

2261
01:32:40.000 --> 01:32:42.490
and Anthony's father was in the passenger seat.

2262
01:32:42.490 --> 01:32:44.090
And I remember reaching around

2263
01:32:44.090 --> 01:32:45.717
and like kind of grabbing his shoulder and said,

2264
01:32:45.717 --> 01:32:47.050
"Hey, Robert, did you know,

2265
01:32:47.050 --> 01:32:49.320
I just finished my first marathon,"

2266
01:32:49.320 --> 01:32:52.670
and just waking up and wishing that that were real.

2267
01:32:52.670 --> 01:32:55.410
That that moment had been real.

2268
01:32:55.410 --> 01:33:00.330
So yeah, it was incredibly gratifying to believe

2269
01:33:00.330 --> 01:33:02.410
or be given the opportunity to believe

2270
01:33:02.410 --> 01:33:04.340
that maybe he had come through.

2271
01:33:04.340 --> 01:33:05.173
Yeah.

2272
01:33:06.130 --> 01:33:08.210
Sounds like an amazing guy.
He was incredible.

2273
01:33:08.210 --> 01:33:09.590
Full-blown Italian, right?

2274
01:33:09.590 --> 01:33:10.718
Yeah. He was born and raised.

2275
01:33:10.718 --> 01:33:11.551
An Italian gentleman.

2276
01:33:11.551 --> 01:33:12.430
Yeah, he was.

2277
01:33:12.430 --> 01:33:15.743
I mean, he was really into cheese, very much into cheese.

2278
01:33:17.004 --> 01:33:19.200
Well he has never tried (indistinct)

2279
01:33:19.200 --> 01:33:21.010
Well, that's very true. That's very true.

2280
01:33:21.010 --> 01:33:23.580
I think we could probably, we could get him there.

2281
01:33:23.580 --> 01:33:24.754
We could.
Yeah.

2282
01:33:24.754 --> 01:33:26.580
He could've come to one of our retreats in Italy.

2283
01:33:26.580 --> 01:33:28.650
Oh, well, we were actually gonna go to your retreat

2284
01:33:28.650 --> 01:33:29.670
until COVID.
(Rich sighs)

2285
01:33:29.670 --> 01:33:31.520
Yeah, we were all signed up.

2286
01:33:31.520 --> 01:33:32.557
I was ready to go. We were all ready.

2287
01:33:32.557 --> 01:33:33.800
Really? I didn't even know that. Oh man.

2288
01:33:33.800 --> 01:33:35.410
Yeah. We were ready to go.

2289
01:33:35.410 --> 01:33:38.010
We were so excited about going to Tuscany.

2290
01:33:38.010 --> 01:33:40.720
Our little Tuscany retreat and then COVID happened.

2291
01:33:40.720 --> 01:33:42.500
We're watching the news and we're like, "Okay.

2292
01:33:42.500 --> 01:33:44.250
I don't think Tuscany's gonna happen."

2293
01:33:44.250 --> 01:33:45.083
Yeah. We're not going to Tuscany.

2294
01:33:45.083 --> 01:33:48.299
I guess I'll start a TikTok.
Yes. Essentially.

2295
01:33:48.299 --> 01:33:50.160
If there was no COVID and you came out on a retreat,

2296
01:33:50.160 --> 01:33:52.270
no TikTok, who knows?
Who knows?

2297
01:33:52.270 --> 01:33:54.360
You never know.

2298
01:33:54.360 --> 01:33:55.348
Yeah. You never know. You never know.

2299
01:33:55.348 --> 01:33:56.940
That's the beautiful thing about it.

