01:57:02.200 --> 01:57:05.223
I was allowed to play violin and do orchestra.

2803
01:57:06.280 --> 01:57:09.080
You know, I remember my junior year in high school,

2804
01:57:09.080 --> 01:57:10.880
that's, you know, really important years

2805
01:57:10.880 --> 01:57:12.120
when you take your SATs.

2806
01:57:12.120 --> 01:57:14.970
And when you're applying for colleges and all that stuff.

2807
01:57:14.970 --> 01:57:18.050
They required me to cut out all extracurricular activities,

2808
01:57:18.050 --> 01:57:21.330
except for like, you know, Model UN, Math club, Latin club,

2809
01:57:21.330 --> 01:57:22.163
the things that would look good

2810
01:57:22.163 --> 01:57:24.730
on your college application, right?

2811
01:57:24.730 --> 01:57:27.570
And even when it was time to go to college,

2812
01:57:27.570 --> 01:57:30.330
they said, we won't pay for college if you major in music.

2813
01:57:30.330 --> 01:57:32.780
Which is what I wanted to study.

2814
01:57:32.780 --> 01:57:34.510
We'll pay for your English degree.

2815
01:57:34.510 --> 01:57:37.670
And even that was a concession, believe me on their part.

2816
01:57:37.670 --> 01:57:40.370
So everything they did was about

2817
01:57:40.370 --> 01:57:43.580
maximizing financial security.
Right.

2818
01:57:43.580 --> 01:57:44.413
And I understand that.

2819
01:57:44.413 --> 01:57:46.140
And failure comes with a capital F, right?

2820
01:57:46.140 --> 01:57:48.310
Absolutely.
So there's a bit of

2821
01:57:48.310 --> 01:57:50.940
deprogramming, you know, when you talk about like,

2822
01:57:50.940 --> 01:57:54.160
don't worry about failure or failure is just, you know,

2823
01:57:54.160 --> 01:57:57.930
a step on the road to, you know, ultimate self-actualization

2824
01:57:57.930 --> 01:57:59.340
or whatever it is,

2825
01:57:59.340 --> 01:58:02.370
like that involves some work on your part.

2826
01:58:02.370 --> 01:58:04.460
That's why I was so scared to hear it.

2827
01:58:04.460 --> 01:58:07.740
I was so terrified to hear that message

2828
01:58:07.740 --> 01:58:11.610
because it was very counter intuitive for me.

2829
01:58:11.610 --> 01:58:13.760
I was like, what are you talking about?

2830
01:58:13.760 --> 01:58:16.060
I got to try and fail 10 million times.

2831
01:58:16.060 --> 01:58:18.190
Like, no, I'm just going to pick the things

2832
01:58:18.190 --> 01:58:20.883
that I know I will win at all the time, you know?

2833
01:58:21.960 --> 01:58:25.190
But I needed to hear it.

2834
01:58:25.190 --> 01:58:27.760
It was the right time for me to hear that message.

2835
01:58:27.760 --> 01:58:29.880
I think I was at a time in my life,

2836
01:58:29.880 --> 01:58:32.100
you know, it was probably about a year and a half ago

2837
01:58:32.100 --> 01:58:33.460
when I listened to it.

2838
01:58:33.460 --> 01:58:36.137
It was at a time in my life where I was like,

2839
01:58:36.137 --> 01:58:37.210
"Is this it for me?

2840
01:58:37.210 --> 01:58:39.510
Is this every day is gonna be like this for me

2841
01:58:39.510 --> 01:58:43.850
until I die, or until I retire, you know, safe little 401k.

2842
01:58:43.850 --> 01:58:45.350
Is that what it is?"

2843
01:58:45.350 --> 01:58:49.170
And the idea that that was what it would be

2844
01:58:49.170 --> 01:58:50.910
was very sad to me.

2845
01:58:50.910 --> 01:58:52.290
I didn't want that.

2846
01:58:52.290 --> 01:58:54.037
So hearing that message that,

2847
01:58:54.037 --> 01:58:56.100
"Hey, you're 40 years old

2848
01:58:56.100 --> 01:58:58.300
and you can totally do something new

2849
01:58:58.300 --> 01:59:00.170
and different and exciting.

2850
01:59:00.170 --> 01:59:03.240
You're still allowed to have dreams at this point,"

2851
01:59:03.240 --> 01:59:07.000
was terrifying, but also electrifying.

2852
01:59:07.000 --> 01:59:09.876
We should call David and let him know.

2853
01:59:09.876 --> 01:59:13.100
He would be very thrilled to hear that.

2854
01:59:13.100 --> 01:59:15.000
That podcast completely, and his book,

2855
01:59:15.000 --> 01:59:17.820
complete radically changed the way that I think.

2856
01:59:17.820 --> 01:59:19.270
Yeah. That's very cool.

2857
01:59:19.270 --> 01:59:22.000
Well, where does that leave you now?

2858
01:59:22.000 --> 01:59:23.360
I mean, selfishly,

2859
01:59:23.360 --> 01:59:27.050
as I think about how challenging your days must be

2860
01:59:27.050 --> 01:59:30.190
trying to balance, you know, wear all of these hats

2861
01:59:30.190 --> 01:59:32.300
and you're not letting yourself off the hook,

2862
01:59:32.300 --> 01:59:34.960
you have to be exceptional in every bucket, you know,

2863
01:59:34.960 --> 01:59:36.720
all the time, right?

2864
01:59:36.720 --> 01:59:37.730
And as I said earlier,

2865
01:59:37.730 --> 01:59:39.911
I do have sustainability in terms about all of this.

2866
01:59:39.911 --> 01:59:42.240
(both laugh)

2867
01:59:42.240 --> 01:59:45.523
Selfishly, and I think a lot of people would agree with me,

2868
01:59:47.616 --> 01:59:50.730
would the world be better with The Korean Vegan

2869
01:59:50.730 --> 01:59:52.363
being the full-time Korean Vegan?

2870
01:59:52.363 --> 01:59:56.150
Like it's got to wear on you when you're making videos

2871
01:59:56.150 --> 01:59:58.100
and knowing that you've got to, you know,

2872
01:59:58.100 --> 01:59:59.690
do these discovery motions

2873
01:59:59.690 --> 02:00:01.740
