Sure, I participate on occasion, but you know what,

3050
02:07:29.000 --> 02:07:32.780
I ultimately started listening to it for was I,

3051
02:07:32.780 --> 02:07:36.640
you know, live in a somewhat siloed community.

3052
02:07:36.640 --> 02:07:40.320
There aren't a lot of Asian-Americans where I live.

3053
02:07:40.320 --> 02:07:42.870
There aren't a lot of black Americans where I live.

3054
02:07:44.420 --> 02:07:47.360
And so what I started doing was just like going into rooms

3055
02:07:47.360 --> 02:07:48.710
with those kinds of people,

3056
02:07:48.710 --> 02:07:51.050
so I could just like, learn about their history,

3057
02:07:51.050 --> 02:07:52.000
what they're talking about.

3058
02:07:52.000 --> 02:07:55.640
What's important to them and being very humble about it

3059
02:07:55.640 --> 02:07:58.410
and being like, I'm just here to learn and to listen.

3060
02:07:58.410 --> 02:08:00.520
Yeah, well, when I look at it for you,

3061
02:08:00.520 --> 02:08:01.353
there's a couple of things.

3062
02:08:01.353 --> 02:08:03.770
First of all, it being a new platform,

3063
02:08:03.770 --> 02:08:06.180
it's always good to get in early on these things,

3064
02:08:06.180 --> 02:08:07.410
as you know, right?
Yes.

3065
02:08:07.410 --> 02:08:10.090
That's where you get that crazy growth arc.

3066
02:08:10.090 --> 02:08:14.220
If you're active on those platforms and providing value.

3067
02:08:14.220 --> 02:08:16.490
But people associate like they associate me

3068
02:08:16.490 --> 02:08:18.360
with conversations, right.

3069
02:08:18.360 --> 02:08:20.740
And this is where they come to this for that.

3070
02:08:20.740 --> 02:08:22.540
So Clubhouse doesn't make a lot of sense,

3071
02:08:22.540 --> 02:08:25.310
but they're used to seeing you making food

3072
02:08:25.310 --> 02:08:26.700
in 60 second clips,

3073
02:08:26.700 --> 02:08:28.210
but what does Joanne look like

3074
02:08:28.210 --> 02:08:31.333
when it's a free form conversation about,

3075
02:08:32.460 --> 02:08:35.240
being a lawyer or being an Asian American lawyer

3076
02:08:35.240 --> 02:08:36.620
or those sorts of things,

3077
02:08:36.620 --> 02:08:38.840
like that's a different version of you

3078
02:08:38.840 --> 02:08:40.990
that I think could be valuable.

3079
02:08:40.990 --> 02:08:43.320
So I think it does make sense for you to do that.

3080
02:08:43.320 --> 02:08:44.153
It could be.

3081
02:08:44.153 --> 02:08:47.340
I mean, but then we go back to this sustainability issue

3082
02:08:47.340 --> 02:08:48.490
and just like... (sighs)

3083
02:08:48.490 --> 02:08:50.120
Right, well, that's why you got to walk away

3084
02:08:50.120 --> 02:08:52.848
from (indistinct) so you could be on Clubhouse.

3085
02:08:52.848 --> 02:08:55.237
(laughs) That's what I'll tell my exit interview,

3086
02:08:55.237 --> 02:08:58.870
"I'm leaving so I can really, explode out Clubhouse."

3087
02:08:58.870 --> 02:09:00.400
They'll love that.

3088
02:09:00.400 --> 02:09:02.910
But yeah, I certainly agree

3089
02:09:02.910 --> 02:09:05.330
that it would be another facet to me.

3090
02:09:05.330 --> 02:09:08.790
And it might be interesting again,

3091
02:09:08.790 --> 02:09:10.380
from a strategic perspective,

3092
02:09:10.380 --> 02:09:13.090
I don't know about Clubhouse's longevity at this point.

3093
02:09:13.090 --> 02:09:14.667
Yeah, I think that's very much in question

3094
02:09:14.667 --> 02:09:15.890
because all these other platforms

3095
02:09:15.890 --> 02:09:16.860
are launching their version of it.

3096
02:09:16.860 --> 02:09:17.693
Exactly.

3097
02:09:17.693 --> 02:09:20.780
And all these other platforms have been through the ringer

3098
02:09:20.780 --> 02:09:23.120
and they know what it takes to survive.

3099
02:09:23.120 --> 02:09:26.190
And you know, I'm not sure that Clubhouse

3100
02:09:26.190 --> 02:09:27.560
is kind of in it for the long haul.

3101
02:09:27.560 --> 02:09:29.880
I'm glad that I participated early on

3102
02:09:29.880 --> 02:09:31.470
for the reasons you described,

3103
02:09:31.470 --> 02:09:33.820
but mostly I'm just really glad for the people I've met

3104
02:09:33.820 --> 02:09:37.400
on Clubhouse, I've met some insanely smart,

3105
02:09:37.400 --> 02:09:38.290
intelligent people.

3106
02:09:38.290 --> 02:09:40.590
Yeah. It is pretty cool.
It is.

3107
02:09:40.590 --> 02:09:43.610
There's a lot to be gained from checking it out.

3108
02:09:43.610 --> 02:09:46.330
Yeah. You should listen to the NFT discussions.

3109
02:09:46.330 --> 02:09:48.710
I guess I should. I have a lot to learn that.

3110
02:09:48.710 --> 02:09:50.290
Although I've talked about it on the podcast.

3111
02:09:50.290 --> 02:09:53.350
[Crosstalk 02:09:50]
I was very impressed.

3112
02:09:53.350 --> 02:09:56.580
I do a little bit of blockchain and crypto stuff

3113
02:09:56.580 --> 02:09:57.950
on the side in my practice.

3114
02:09:57.950 --> 02:10:00.050
I was very impressed by your knowledge level.

3115
02:10:00.050 --> 02:10:01.550
Oh thank you.

3116
02:10:01.550 --> 02:10:03.650
We can't end this without talking a little bit

3117
02:10:03.650 --> 02:10:05.920
about the vegan aspect of all of this.

3118
02:10:05.920 --> 02:10:07.300
Like, I feel like we've given that

3119
02:10:07.300 --> 02:10:08.380
a little bit of short shrift.

3120
02:10:08.380 --> 02:10:12.173
I mean, Anthony, you know, got into it

3121
02:10:12.173 --> 02:10:14.660
from a health perspective that was initially

3122
02:10:14.660 --> 02:10:15.620
an impetus for you.

3123
02:10:15.620 --> 02:10:18.480
And then it became about the environment and compassion,

3124
02:10:18.480 --> 02:10:20.640
but how has that evolved?

3125
02:10:20.640 --> 02:10:22.140
How do you think about it now?

3126
02:10:23.030 --> 02:10:25.140
And for somebody who's listening, like,

3127
02:10:25.140 --> 02:10:26.810
look, there's a lot of vegans and plant-based people

3128
02:10:26.810 --> 02:10:29.330
that listen to us, but I would say by and large,

3129
02:10:29.330 --> 02:10:33.490
like the vast majority of them are perhaps plant curious

3130
02:10:33.490 --> 02:10:35.650
or interested, but not really.

3131
02:10:35.650 --> 02:10:39.560
They're like, how do you communicate with somebody

3132
02:10:39.560 --> 02:10:42.790
who's flirting with the idea of stepping into this

3133
02:10:42.790 --> 02:10:45.020
in a more meaningful way.

3134
02:10:45.020 --> 02:10:47.910
So I would start where I always start,

3135
02:10:47.910 --> 02:10:50.280
which is just my personal story,

3136
02:10:50.280 --> 02:10:54.070
because I don't want anyone to think that I've got an agenda

3137
02:10:54.070 --> 02:10:58.630
with what I'm sharing and what I'm sharing is very simple.

3138
02:10:58.630 --> 02:11:01.110
You know, I started out, as you said, for you know,

3139
02:11:01.110 --> 02:11:03.610
health reasons and environmental reasons.

3140
02:11:03.610 --> 02:11:05.840
Those two things were very compelling to me.

3141
02:11:05.840 --> 02:11:09.140
Missing from the analysis was any idea

3142
02:11:09.140 --> 02:11:10.930
of compassion for animals,

3143
02:11:10.930 --> 02:11:15.380
which is very strange because I've always loved animals.

3144
02:11:15.380 --> 02:11:18.600
Like I'm one of those persons who can't watch animal planet,

3145
02:11:18.600 --> 02:11:19.670
because I'm always worried

3146
02:11:19.670 --> 02:11:21.360
that something's being done to the animals.

3147
02:11:21.360 --> 02:11:24.773
I can't stand watching animals get hurt.

3148
02:11:25.835 --> 02:11:28.640
And so that was completely absent

3149
02:11:28.640 --> 02:11:31.070
from my decision making process.

3150
02:11:31.070 --> 02:11:34.210
But I remember the last thing I ate before I went vegan

3151
02:11:34.210 --> 02:11:35.590
was a fried chicken sandwich.

3152
02:11:35.590 --> 02:11:38.044
It used to be one of my favorite things to eat.

3153
02:11:38.044 --> 02:11:40.040
And there was a restaurant right next to my house

3154
02:11:40.040 --> 02:11:42.670
that had delicious fried chicken sandwiches.

3155
02:11:42.670 --> 02:11:44.140
And I was like, "Oh man, this is the last time

3156
02:11:44.140 --> 02:11:47.070
I'm gonna eat this, oh, well that sucks," right?

3157
02:11:47.070 --> 02:11:49.900
A couple of weeks later, or maybe even longer than that,

3158
02:11:49.900 --> 02:11:52.020
a few, probably several weeks later,

3159
02:11:52.020 --> 02:11:53.500
I'm walking past that restaurant

3160
02:11:53.500 --> 02:11:55.420
and I can smell that fried chicken sandwich.

3161
02:11:55.420 --> 02:11:58.400
And I'm like, "Oh man, well, nobody's watching.

3162
02:11:58.400 --> 02:11:59.970
I could just go in and eat it.

3163
02:11:59.970 --> 02:12:02.120
I won't even have to tell Anthony."

3164
02:12:02.120 --> 02:12:07.120
And it wasn't being caught that stopped me.

3165
02:12:07.260 --> 02:12:10.430
What stopped me was me thinking of

3166
02:12:10.430 --> 02:12:14.810
what do the chickens have to go through for me to have this,

3167
02:12:14.810 --> 02:12:19.560
what, seven minutes enjoyment of this chicken sandwich?

3168
02:12:19.560 --> 02:12:22.760
And I was like, well, it's an easy answer then.

3169
02:12:22.760 --> 02:12:24.150
Absolutely easy answer.

3170
02:12:24.150 --> 02:12:26.420
Like why would the chickens have to go through this

3171
02:12:26.420 --> 02:12:28.900
for their whole lives so that I can enjoy

3172
02:12:28.900 --> 02:12:30.180
a seven minute chicken sandwich,

3173
02:12:30.180 --> 02:12:32.350
which is gonna be terrible for me anyway.

3174
02:12:32.350 --> 02:12:34.080
Like that just rationally speaking

3175
02:12:34.080 --> 02:12:36.930
doesn't make any sense to me at all.

3176
02:12:36.930 --> 02:12:38.440
And in that moment,

3177
02:12:38.440 --> 02:12:43.440
what I realized was that somehow this kind of locked up,

3178
02:12:44.460 --> 02:12:48.090
pent up compassion and love I had for animals

3179
02:12:48.090 --> 02:12:51.410
was completely broken free and liberated

3180
02:12:51.410 --> 02:12:53.400
as a result of my decision.

3181
02:12:53.400 --> 02:12:56.850
And all of a sudden I felt like, oh my God,

3182
02:12:56.850 --> 02:12:58.610
I can now love animals

3183
02:12:58.610 --> 02:13:01.580
as much as I always wanted to love them.

3184
02:13:01.580 --> 02:13:04.600
Because before I was like, "Well, I love animals,

3185
02:13:04.600 --> 02:13:06.860
but I love my bacon cheeseburger sandwich."

3186
02:13:06.860 --> 02:13:09.510
You know, it was always stopped by that,

3187
02:13:09.510 --> 02:13:12.110
but there was no longer that stopping me.

3188
02:13:12.110 --> 02:13:15.740
And that was the most liberating, wonderful feeling.

3189
02:13:15.740 --> 02:13:19.250
I felt like this huge weight had been lifted off of me.

3190
02:13:19.250 --> 02:13:20.397
And so when people ask me,

3191
02:13:20.397 --> 02:13:22.890
"What is the biggest benefit you've ever received

3192
02:13:22.890 --> 02:13:23.880
from going vegan?"

3193
02:13:23.880 --> 02:13:24.910
It's that.

3194
02:13:24.910 --> 02:13:27.877
It's that feeling that when I look at my dogs, I can say,

3195
02:13:27.877 --> 02:13:31.190
"I love you with every inch of my heart."

3196
02:13:31.190 --> 02:13:34.390
There's nothing being reserved for bacon or cheeseburgers

3197
02:13:34.390 --> 02:13:36.627
or anything like that, it's all for you.

3198
02:13:36.627 --> 02:13:39.520
And that feeling is so wonderful.

3199
02:13:39.520 --> 02:13:42.650
Does that resonate with everyone? Sometimes it does.

3200
02:13:42.650 --> 02:13:44.340
Sometimes it doesn't.

3201
02:13:44.340 --> 02:13:47.950
But at least it's like 100% truthful.

3202
02:13:47.950 --> 02:13:50.010
And I think people pick up on that.

3203
02:13:50.010 --> 02:13:52.933
Yeah, that's a really interesting way to put it.

3204
02:13:54.280 --> 02:13:58.440
In furtherance to that, I think the idea behind it is

3205
02:13:58.440 --> 02:14:01.750
how do you live your life more in alignment

3206
02:14:01.750 --> 02:14:03.400
with your values?

3207
02:14:03.400 --> 02:14:05.420
I think most people, I think what you spoke about

3208
02:14:05.420 --> 02:14:07.000
is a very common thing.

3209
02:14:07.000 --> 02:14:09.700
Like we love animals, but we love our bacon cheeseburger.

3210
02:14:09.700 --> 02:14:13.220
And we find a way to reconcile that and just move forward

3211
02:14:13.220 --> 02:14:15.120
and not worry about it too much.

3212
02:14:15.120 --> 02:14:19.790
But that inconsistency, that incongruency

3213
02:14:19.790 --> 02:14:21.280
has a stress, impact.

3214
02:14:21.280 --> 02:14:23.427
I think any time when you're saying one thing

3215
02:14:23.427 --> 02:14:24.550
and doing another,

3216
02:14:24.550 --> 02:14:28.710
you're creating that a little dissonance inside yourself

3217
02:14:28.710 --> 02:14:31.100
that wears on your soul, on some level

3218
02:14:31.100 --> 02:14:33.020
and you pay a toll for that.

3219
02:14:33.020 --> 02:14:37.170
And that might be so minute that it's just a tiny whisper

3220
02:14:37.170 --> 02:14:40.340
and you can just continue to live on, you know, blindly

3221
02:14:40.340 --> 02:14:41.630
without paying attention to it.

3222
02:14:41.630 --> 02:14:43.270
But there is something about,

3223
02:14:43.270 --> 02:14:46.120
and I just know this in my own experience,

3224
02:14:46.120 --> 02:14:48.360
continuing to iterate on this over the years,

3225
02:14:48.360 --> 02:14:50.360
that every time I identify one of those things

3226
02:14:50.360 --> 02:14:52.730
and have the courage to stop doing that thing,

3227
02:14:52.730 --> 02:14:54.550
that doesn't match up with what I believe

3228
02:14:54.550 --> 02:14:57.530
or what I'm telling other people, there is a lightness.

3229
02:14:57.530 --> 02:15:00.650
You just feel a little bit lighter in your shoes,

3230
02:15:00.650 --> 02:15:02.910
and that allows you to kind of walk into a room

3231
02:15:02.910 --> 02:15:04.860
and look at somebody in the eye

3232
02:15:04.860 --> 02:15:07.600
and just feel more comfortable in your own skin.

3233
02:15:07.600 --> 02:15:12.600
A big part of sobriety, that journey is that reconciliation.

3234
02:15:12.620 --> 02:15:15.870
And so I think that our relationship to animals

3235
02:15:15.870 --> 02:15:20.870
and our food is symbolically very similar in that regard.

3236
02:15:20.910 --> 02:15:25.910
I think that it is about intentionality, right?

3237
02:15:26.530 --> 02:15:28.700
You can't be intentional about something

3238
02:15:28.700 --> 02:15:31.760
if you spend your whole life denying it

3239
02:15:31.760 --> 02:15:33.950
and pretending it doesn't exist.

3240
02:15:33.950 --> 02:15:35.830
And that's what I think we're taught to do.

3241
02:15:35.830 --> 02:15:39.940
We're conditioned to just shove this dissonance, as you say,

3242
02:15:39.940 --> 02:15:42.410
put it away, don't think about it

3243
02:15:42.410 --> 02:15:44.670
and just deny its existence

3244
02:15:44.670 --> 02:15:48.310
and therefore your consumption of animal products,

3245
02:15:48.310 --> 02:15:50.230
whether it's by eating or otherwise,

3246
02:15:50.230 --> 02:15:51.800
is completely unintentional

3247
02:15:51.800 --> 02:15:55.260
because you won't even acknowledge its existence, right.

3248
02:15:55.260 --> 02:15:59.550
And so, you know, when I think about how do I live

3249
02:15:59.550 --> 02:16:04.470
such that my actions are more consistent with my values,

3250
02:16:04.470 --> 02:16:06.680
you need to be honest about it.

3251
02:16:06.680 --> 02:16:09.420
And that is the beginning of it.

3252
02:16:09.420 --> 02:16:12.800
But I think it's also just understanding

3253
02:16:12.800 --> 02:16:15.800
that you can't be perfect at it, right?

3254
02:16:15.800 --> 02:16:17.340
Like, you know, I always tell people

3255
02:16:17.340 --> 02:16:19.540
there's no such thing as perfect vegan, right?

3256
02:16:19.540 --> 02:16:22.500
It's not possible in the way that our world

3257
02:16:22.500 --> 02:16:25.680
is currently structured to completely 100%

3258
02:16:25.680 --> 02:16:27.560
avoid all animal products

3259
02:16:27.560 --> 02:16:30.008
in every aspect of your life, right?

3260
02:16:30.008 --> 02:16:32.440
But-
But the minute you dip

3261
02:16:32.440 --> 02:16:33.890
your toe in the wrong way,

3262
02:16:33.890 --> 02:16:35.610
the vegans are the first to let you know

3263
02:16:35.610 --> 02:16:36.443
that you did it wrong.

3264
02:16:36.443 --> 02:16:39.110
Yes. Oh, believe me on TikTok. Yeah.

3265
02:16:39.110 --> 02:16:40.760
That's for sure.

3266
02:16:40.760 --> 02:16:42.580
You know, I use a lot of egg replacer

3267
02:16:42.580 --> 02:16:45.930
in a lot of my cooking because, in Korean cuisine,

3268
02:16:45.930 --> 02:16:48.170
like (indistinct) is a big thing, right.

3269
02:16:48.170 --> 02:16:52.090
And always indubitably, they're like egg isn't vegan.

3270
02:16:52.090 --> 02:16:55.100
I'm like, what part of egg replacer

3271
02:16:55.100 --> 02:16:58.220
is so difficult for you to understand, you know?

3272
02:16:58.220 --> 02:17:01.410
And also I'm The Korean Vegan, everything I make is vegan.

3273
02:17:01.410 --> 02:17:04.710
Or in the first iteration of that replacement product,

3274
02:17:04.710 --> 02:17:07.170
they did some animal testing or something like that.

3275
02:17:07.170 --> 02:17:09.010
So that's off the table.

3276
02:17:09.010 --> 02:17:11.610
Like how far down this rabbit hole are you gonna go?

3277
02:17:11.610 --> 02:17:13.950
I mean, when they mulched the fields

3278
02:17:13.950 --> 02:17:16.030
to plant the vegetables,

3279
02:17:16.030 --> 02:17:19.050
some insects are getting killed or some worms or some mice

3280
02:17:19.050 --> 02:17:20.350
or something like that-
Or when you ride

3281
02:17:20.350 --> 02:17:21.900
your bicycle.

3282
02:17:21.900 --> 02:17:25.103
Back to Jeong Kwan, who I'm mispronouncing again.

3283
02:17:25.103 --> 02:17:27.470
It's okay.
None of us are living

3284
02:17:27.470 --> 02:17:30.450
a harm-free life of perfect ahimsa.

3285
02:17:30.450 --> 02:17:31.890
We're all producing harm.

3286
02:17:31.890 --> 02:17:35.180
It's about your intention and minimizing that

3287
02:17:35.180 --> 02:17:37.511
to the best of your ability

3288
02:17:37.511 --> 02:17:39.750
without murdering yourself either.

3289
02:17:39.750 --> 02:17:40.660
Right, well, I mean,

3290
02:17:40.660 --> 02:17:42.980
that was one of the most lovely things

3291
02:17:42.980 --> 02:17:44.930
I heard from Jeong Kwan Sunim is,

3292
02:17:44.930 --> 02:17:48.170
she was like, when you harm somebody else,

3293
02:17:48.170 --> 02:17:51.370
you're harming yourself as much, right?

3294
02:17:51.370 --> 02:17:53.349
And so there's this energy transaction-

3295
02:17:53.349 --> 02:17:54.660
That speaks to that dissonance as well. Yeah.

3296
02:17:54.660 --> 02:17:56.270
Exactly. Exactly.

3297
02:17:56.270 --> 02:18:00.610
So you are harming yourself when you're eating like that

3298
02:18:00.610 --> 02:18:02.930
or consuming like that in that way.

3299
02:18:02.930 --> 02:18:04.040
And again,

3300
02:18:04.040 --> 02:18:08.100
the intention has to not be the complete eradication

3301
02:18:08.100 --> 02:18:11.620
of impact or harm, because I don't think that's possible,

3302
02:18:11.620 --> 02:18:15.670
but it's to make that as small as possible

3303
02:18:15.670 --> 02:18:17.500
while of course recognizing

3304
02:18:17.500 --> 02:18:19.520
that you're part of that equation, right.

3305
02:18:19.520 --> 02:18:23.190
And so that's why I think it's more a question of intention

3306
02:18:23.190 --> 02:18:26.263
than it is about whether you check all the boxes.

3307
02:18:26.263 --> 02:18:28.350
Yeah. Yeah.

3308
02:18:28.350 --> 02:18:32.010
So what's the first thing somebody who's listening

3309
02:18:32.010 --> 02:18:35.963
or watching can do to begin to make that switch?

3310
02:18:37.270 --> 02:18:39.950
I think the first thing they can do

3311
02:18:39.950 --> 02:18:41.767
is probably just identify,

3312
02:18:41.767 --> 02:18:46.767
"Hey, what's one meal or one food

3313
02:18:47.070 --> 02:18:50.670
that I can maybe replace with something else?"

3314
02:18:50.670 --> 02:18:53.410
Not all the time, but once in a while.

3315
02:18:53.410 --> 02:18:58.300
So for example, you know, I love the prominence now

3316
02:18:58.300 --> 02:19:00.780
of Beyond Burgers and Impossible Meats,

3317
02:19:00.780 --> 02:19:02.790
because there are a lot of people who are like, "Yeah no,

3318
02:19:02.790 --> 02:19:06.580
I can't live without can't, live without my hamburger,

3319
02:19:06.580 --> 02:19:11.220
or I can't live without my sausages or whatnot."

3320
02:19:11.220 --> 02:19:13.020
And hey, you know what?

3321
02:19:13.020 --> 02:19:16.170
The great thing is technology has evolved to a point

3322
02:19:16.170 --> 02:19:19.820
where you maybe don't need to live without your sausage,

3323
02:19:19.820 --> 02:19:22.300
just replace it with an alternative.

3324
02:19:22.300 --> 02:19:24.410
So I always say like,

3325
02:19:24.410 --> 02:19:27.320
think a little bit, think in small steps,

3326
02:19:27.320 --> 02:19:30.760
you do not need to eradicate all animal products

3327
02:19:30.760 --> 02:19:32.580
from your diet tomorrow.

3328
02:19:32.580 --> 02:19:34.490
Nobody is asking you to do that.

3329
02:19:34.490 --> 02:19:36.080
Well, maybe some people are asking you to that.

3330
02:19:36.080 --> 02:19:37.790
I'm not asking you to do that.

3331
02:19:37.790 --> 02:19:39.850
I'm asking you to say, "Hey, you know what,

3332
02:19:39.850 --> 02:19:42.950
next time I make lamian or ramen noodles,

3333
02:19:42.950 --> 02:19:45.090
I'm not gonna put an egg in it

3334
02:19:45.090 --> 02:19:46.550
and I'm gonna buy the vegan one

3335
02:19:46.550 --> 02:19:48.010
'cause it tastes just as delicious

3336
02:19:48.010 --> 02:19:49.630
and it tastes just as good.

3337
02:19:49.630 --> 02:19:53.580
And you know, maybe instead of having bacon with my pizza,

3338
02:19:53.580 --> 02:19:54.413
you know what?

3339
02:19:54.413 --> 02:19:55.560
I'm gonna cut out all the meat

3340
02:19:55.560 --> 02:19:57.420
and just stick to cheese for now.

3341
02:19:57.420 --> 02:19:59.650
And then maybe one day I'll actually replace it

3342
02:19:59.650 --> 02:20:02.300
with vegan cheese because it's so fricking good now.

3343
02:20:02.300 --> 02:20:04.760
So it's more like baby steps, as you said,

3344
02:20:04.760 --> 02:20:06.480
instead of trying to get them

3345
02:20:06.480 --> 02:20:09.540
to completely change their lives in one 60 second post.

3346
02:20:09.540 --> 02:20:10.730
Right, but ultimately,

3347
02:20:10.730 --> 02:20:13.060
it's about attraction over promotion, right?

3348
02:20:13.060 --> 02:20:14.750
When you watch your videos,

3349
02:20:14.750 --> 02:20:17.140
what you're preparing is so much better

3350
02:20:17.140 --> 02:20:19.170
than what any of us are eating anyway.

3351
02:20:19.170 --> 02:20:20.270
And you're like, it doesn't matter

3352
02:20:20.270 --> 02:20:21.660
if there's meat in that thing or not

3353
02:20:21.660 --> 02:20:23.470
because like, I need that now.

3354
02:20:23.470 --> 02:20:25.200
I think that's exactly...

3355
02:20:25.200 --> 02:20:28.860
So I, whether you call it sneaky, strategic, calculating,

3356
02:20:28.860 --> 02:20:33.860
I am very, again strategic, about how I share my veganism.

3357
02:20:35.830 --> 02:20:39.757
I feel like if you just go out there and just tell them,

3358
02:20:39.757 --> 02:20:43.160
"This is what you need to eat or this is how you need to be.

3359
02:20:43.160 --> 02:20:44.880
The world is burning all around you.

3360
02:20:44.880 --> 02:20:47.000
Why are you eating that way?"

3361
02:20:47.000 --> 02:20:48.450
I think there's a place for that.

3362
02:20:48.450 --> 02:20:49.890
And I think there are some hearts

3363
02:20:49.890 --> 02:20:51.430
that are receptive to that.

3364
02:20:51.430 --> 02:20:53.420
And therefore, I know you had Maggie Kwon

3365
02:20:53.420 --> 02:20:55.820
a couple of weeks ago or something.

3366
02:20:55.820 --> 02:20:57.520
And she said it really well,

3367
02:20:57.520 --> 02:21:01.170
she's like, "There's a place for every kind of activism."

3368
02:21:01.170 --> 02:21:04.400
But my kind of activism is not in your face.

3369
02:21:04.400 --> 02:21:05.900
It's more sneaky than that.

3370
02:21:05.900 --> 02:21:08.770
It's like, "Hey, look at what I'm making,

3371
02:21:08.770 --> 02:21:10.770
doesn't it look so delicious?

3372
02:21:10.770 --> 02:21:13.510
Oh and by the way, it happens to be animal free.

3373
02:21:13.510 --> 02:21:15.520
And it's really, really good."

3374
02:21:15.520 --> 02:21:17.790
I love hearing from my TikTok fans.

3375
02:21:17.790 --> 02:21:19.710
Oh my God, I had no idea you were vegan,

3376
02:21:19.710 --> 02:21:20.882
even though it says the Korean Vegan.

3377
02:21:20.882 --> 02:21:21.973
It's the Korean Vegan.

3378
02:21:21.973 --> 02:21:22.806
(both laugh)

3379
02:21:22.806 --> 02:21:24.320
I get it all the time.

3380
02:21:24.320 --> 02:21:26.160
They're like, "I have been following you for months.

3381
02:21:26.160 --> 02:21:27.500
I had no idea you were vegan."

3382
02:21:27.500 --> 02:21:30.060
That's so funny.
I love that. I love that.

3383
02:21:30.060 --> 02:21:31.143
Yeah. Yeah.

3384
02:21:32.770 --> 02:21:36.350
That is attraction over promotion because

3385
02:21:36.350 --> 02:21:38.950
look, nobody wants to be brow beat.

3386
02:21:38.950 --> 02:21:40.700
Nobody wants their inventory taken.

3387
02:21:40.700 --> 02:21:43.050
Nobody wants to be told how they're doing it wrong.

3388
02:21:43.050 --> 02:21:46.680
What they want is something that is alluring.

3389
02:21:46.680 --> 02:21:50.060
And the fact that you cast this tractor beam

3390
02:21:50.060 --> 02:21:53.310
and draw all these people in with your storytelling

3391
02:21:53.310 --> 02:21:56.040
and your beautiful photography and these videos,

3392
02:21:56.040 --> 02:21:58.390
it's really a magical thing that you're doing.

3393
02:21:58.390 --> 02:21:59.787
Oh thank you. Very much.
It really is a beautiful

3394
02:21:59.787 --> 02:22:00.620
thing.

3395
02:22:01.987 --> 02:22:03.310
And I wish you well.

3396
02:22:03.310 --> 02:22:05.577
Oh thank you. I wish you very well too.

3397
02:22:06.510 --> 02:22:09.280
If there's anything I can do to help you at any time,

3398
02:22:09.280 --> 02:22:10.210
I love what you're doing.

3399
02:22:10.210 --> 02:22:12.870
You're impacting so many people and it's powerful.

3400
02:22:12.870 --> 02:22:14.450
It's really, really powerful.

3401
02:22:14.450 --> 02:22:18.020
And I like want you so badly to take that in

3402
02:22:18.020 --> 02:22:20.000
when you were talking about imposter syndrome

3403
02:22:20.000 --> 02:22:21.050
and like, "Why do..."

3404
02:22:21.980 --> 02:22:24.020
Please disabuse yourself of that notion

3405
02:22:24.020 --> 02:22:26.660
like you are doing what you're meant to be doing.

3406
02:22:26.660 --> 02:22:28.530
You're carrying a really powerful resonance

3407
02:22:28.530 --> 02:22:29.870
and you're making a difference.

3408
02:22:29.870 --> 02:22:32.270
Well, that means a lot coming from the man

3409
02:22:32.270 --> 02:22:34.209
who's probably responsible for The Korean Vegan.

3410
02:22:34.209 --> 02:22:38.147
No. No. I can't even process that. That trips me out.

3411
02:22:39.150 --> 02:22:42.270
Yeah. It's literally a dream come true to be here.

3412
02:22:42.270 --> 02:22:45.297
I've literally, from the moment we went vegan, I was like,

3413
02:22:45.297 --> 02:22:47.370
"One day I will meet Rich Roll

3414
02:22:47.370 --> 02:22:50.330
and I will tell him how much he changed my life."

3415
02:22:50.330 --> 02:22:51.989
Wow. That's beautiful.

3416
02:22:51.989 --> 02:22:55.010
And you're a powerful manifester. Look what you create.

3417
02:22:55.010 --> 02:22:55.843
Yeah, I know.

3418
02:22:55.843 --> 02:22:57.840
With your powerful mind.
It's amazing.

3419
02:22:57.840 --> 02:22:59.720
It's amazing what we can all create

3420
02:22:59.720 --> 02:23:02.640
if we just believe in ourselves a little bit.

3421
02:23:02.640 --> 02:23:05.771
Yeah. I love it. I think we did it.

3422
02:23:05.771 --> 02:23:06.604
Yay!

3423
02:23:06.604 --> 02:23:07.860
How do you feel?
I feel great.

3424
02:23:07.860 --> 02:23:08.880
I feel good.
This is good right?

3425
02:23:08.880 --> 02:23:10.090
Yeah. It was good.

3426
02:23:10.090 --> 02:23:11.338
I hope it was good.

3427
02:23:11.338 --> 02:23:12.810
Yeah. It was really good.

3428
02:23:12.810 --> 02:23:15.240
You are welcome anytime at my table,

3429
02:23:15.240 --> 02:23:17.330
but I would like to enjoy your food.

3430
02:23:17.330 --> 02:23:18.500
You brought me Korean food.

3431
02:23:18.500 --> 02:23:20.190
Yes. I brought you (indistinct)

3432
02:23:20.190 --> 02:23:23.637
I actually consulted with my family on what to make for you,

3433
02:23:24.622 --> 02:23:26.240
'cause I was like, "Okay, he's really healthy.

3434
02:23:26.240 --> 02:23:29.410
And he's an athlete, but you know, he's not Korean.

3435
02:23:29.410 --> 02:23:30.710
So I don't know how much experience

3436
02:23:30.710 --> 02:23:31.543
he has with Korean food.

3437
02:23:31.543 --> 02:23:32.376
And I also have to find something

3438
02:23:32.376 --> 02:23:33.620
that I can make the day before

3439
02:23:33.620 --> 02:23:35.450
and will still taste good the next day."

3440
02:23:35.450 --> 02:23:37.650
So we went through a number of different options

3441
02:23:37.650 --> 02:23:40.030
and we ultimately decided that braised tofu

3442
02:23:40.030 --> 02:23:42.310
was the best option and it's in my cookbook.

3443
02:23:42.310 --> 02:23:43.240
So it's directly out of there.

3444
02:23:43.240 --> 02:23:45.100
Well, I can't wait to try it.

3445
02:23:45.100 --> 02:23:46.600
So thank you for that.
It's yummy.

3446
02:23:46.600 --> 02:23:47.570
In the meantime,

3447
02:23:47.570 --> 02:23:50.680
everybody pick up The Korean Vegan Cookbook.

3448
02:23:50.680 --> 02:23:52.040
This thing's gonna crush it.

3449
02:23:52.040 --> 02:23:52.873
Thank you. I'm very excited.

3450
02:23:52.873 --> 02:23:54.110
Are you ready? Are you ready?

3451
02:23:54.110 --> 02:23:57.620
I'm very ready for it to crush people. (laughs)

3452
02:23:57.620 --> 02:23:59.400
It's an amazing work of art

3453
02:23:59.400 --> 02:24:02.430
and I think it's gonna transform even more lives.

3454
02:24:02.430 --> 02:24:04.530
So come back and talk to me again sometime.

3455
02:24:04.530 --> 02:24:05.660
I will, thank you.

3456
02:24:05.660 --> 02:24:07.660
In the meantime, everybody knows where to find you,

3457
02:24:07.660 --> 02:24:12.220
just type in The Korean Vegan into your internet machine

3458
02:24:12.220 --> 02:24:14.070
and all sorts of stuff will pop up

3459
02:24:14.070 --> 02:24:16.133
and your life will never be the same.

3460
02:24:16.133 --> 02:24:17.768
Yes. Yes.
All right.

3461
02:24:17.768 --> 02:24:19.407
Peace, plants.

3462
02:24:19.407 --> 02:24:21.990
(gentle music)

